CAT = "fiMarkings"; SEG = "MRK"
Q = [
('You see a continuous yellow line along the middle of a Finnish road. What does its colour tell you?',
 'It divides opposing traffic', ['It marks a cycle lane', 'It marks a bus lane', 'It marks a parking zone'],
 'Finland marks the lines between opposite traffic flows in yellow. White lines separate lanes going the same way and mark edges.'),
("What does a continuous line in the middle of the road mean?",
 "Do not cross or drive on it", ["Overtake with extra care", "Bus lane ahead", "Lane for turning only"],
 "A continuous line (sulkuviiva) must not be crossed or straddled. It is often used where overtaking would be dangerous."),
("The dashes of the centre line become much longer and the gaps shorter. What is this telling you?",
 "A solid line or danger ahead", ["A bus stop on the right ahead", "End of the road", "A cycle lane ahead"],
 "A warning line has longer dashes and shorter gaps than a normal centre line. It tells you a continuous line or a risky stretch is coming."),
("There is a continuous line on your side and a broken line on the other side of it. May you cross?",
 "No, not from your side", ["Yes, from either side", "Yes, to overtake quickly", "Only in daylight"],
 "With a double line you may cross only from the side with the broken line. A continuous line on your side means you stay in your lane."),
('A STOP sign and a stop line stand before a railway level crossing with no barriers. What must you do?',
 'Stop at the line and look', ['Slow down, then cross', 'Stop only if a train shows', 'Cross at walking pace'],
 'At a STOP sign you must stop at the stop line every time, then cross only when you have made sure no train is coming.'),
('A row of white triangles across your lane marks a give-way line. If you must stop, where do you stop?',
 'Just before the triangles', ['On the triangles', 'Past the triangles', 'Level with the sign'],
 "The triangles, known as shark's teeth, mark where you must give way. If you need to stop, stop before them."),
("Lane arrows show your lane turns left only, but you want to go straight. What should you do?",
 "Turn left as marked", ["Go straight on anyway", "Stop and reverse", "Straddle two lanes"],
 "Once in a lane marked by arrows you must follow them. Choose the right lane in good time; if you are wrong, follow the arrow and find a new route."),
("Both the red and the yellow lights are on at once. What happens next?",
 "Green comes on soon", ["Red comes on soon", "The lights are faulty", "Only trams may go"],
 "Red and yellow together mean the light is about to turn green. Get ready, but do not move off until green shows."),
("The light turns yellow when you are a few metres from the stop line, too close to stop without braking hard. What should you do?",
 "Drive on through with care", ["Brake hard to stop at once", "Stop beyond the stop line", "Reverse behind the line"],
 "Yellow means stop before the stop line, unless you are so close that you could not stop safely."),
("Late at night the lights at a junction flash yellow, and a give-way sign stands on your side. Who goes first?",
 "Crossing traffic, as signed", ["You, the light is not red", "Whoever comes from the right", "Whoever arrives first"],
 "Flashing yellow means the lights are not controlling traffic, only warning. The signs and the general rules apply, so the give-way sign decides."),
('A separate green arrow for turning right goes dark while the round light stays red. What does that mean?',
 'The round red light applies', ['You may still turn right', 'Turn right with care', 'Go straight on instead'],
 'A green arrow lets traffic go in its direction only while it is lit. When it goes out, the round red light applies to you.'),
("Lights are mounted over each lane of a road. Which light applies to you?",
 "The one over your lane", ["The one on the right-hand side", "The brightest one", "Any green one"],
 "When signals are placed lane by lane above the road, each light applies only to vehicles using that lane."),
("A pedestrian crosses at lights with a pedestrian signal. Which light must they follow?",
 "The pedestrian signal", ["The light for vehicles", "Whichever light is green", "No light at all"],
 "Pedestrians follow pedestrian signals first, and the vehicle lights for their direction only where there is no pedestrian signal."),
("A police officer stands with one arm raised straight up. What does it mean?",
 "Stop, unless already past", ["Go straight on", "Speed up and clear the junction", "Turn right only"],
 "An arm raised straight up means stop for all approaching traffic, except drivers who could no longer stop safely."),
("A police officer faces you with an arm stretched out to the side. What should you do?",
 "Stop", ["Drive on", "Turn left", "Reverse"],
 "Traffic facing the front or back of an officer with arms stretched sideways must stop. Traffic moving parallel to the arms may go."),
("Which take priority over all other traffic controls?",
 "Signals from a police officer", ["Traffic lights", "Road signs and their panels", "Road markings"],
 "A road user must follow signs, orders and bans given by a traffic controller first, even if they differ from lights, signs or markings."),
]
